scope: |
  Direct continuation of `corpus-contract-shard-fix` (released 098cb8ff1): finish the two REAL bugs
  that gate found, so the Corpus Contract can go fully green for the first time and SPRINT E6
  (re-baseline) becomes mechanical. Final run 30285845478 already has shard 2/4 GREEN and only 5
  non-PASS left; these two bugs are 3 of those 5.

  1. `coroutine-demo-import-cycle-on-interpreter`. `examples/coroutine-demo.ssc` cannot run on INT
     (`Import cycle detected: coroutine.ssc → coroutine.ssc`), which SKIPs the case on EVERY lane
     because INT is the golden. Root cause: `v1/runtime/std/coroutine.ssc` re-imports ITSELF in its
     literate example blocks (lines 44/63/82); the cycle detector at SectionRuntime.scala:382 is
     correct and catches it. Planned fix = treat a DIRECT self-import as a no-op: `moduleLoading` is
     a LinkedHashSet (insertion-ordered), so `moduleLoading.lastOption == Some(resolvedPath)` is
     exactly "this module is importing itself" — vacuous by construction (the names are already in
     scope). A longer A→B→A cycle must STILL error. Fall back to fixing coroutine.ssc's blocks if
     the resolver change shows any conformance fallout.
  2. `rozum-agent-schema-derived-js-and-v2-gaps`. js: `not callable` from the generated .cjs;
     v2: native front emits the `_err` parser sentinel. Pin the v2 `_err` to a concrete construct
     first. The case also binds a fixed port, so `corpus-skip.txt` on documented non-hermetic
     grounds is a legitimate outcome — but only as a judgement about the CASE, never to make the
     gate green.
  3. Then SPRINT E6: `contract.sc --update-baseline` UNSHARDED, one line per entry saying whether it
     is documented state or a bug that stays red.
  ⚠️ OVERLAP WATCH: `js-char-into-int-param` (live, opus) is also in the v1 JS backend. I will not
  touch v1 JS codegen until that claim releases; the js half of item 2 waits behind it.
